          "pull_request": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ezefernandezyf/fastify/pulls/1",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/ezefernandezyf/fastify/pull/1",
            "diff_url": "https://github.com/ezefernandezyf/fastify/pull/1.diff",
            "patch_url": "https://github.com/ezefernandezyf/fastify/pull/1.patch",
            "merged_at": null
          },
          "body": "Fixes #7043\r\n\r\n## What to review first\r\n1. `lib/server.js`: the `{ server, closePromise }` binding shape and `closeSecondary` resolving the promise (this is the root cause fix).\r\n2. `fastify.js` close block: `done()` now gates on `Promise.all` of secondary close promises.\r\n3. `test/close.test.js`: the regression test (request in-flight on the IPv4 secondary listener when `close()` is called).\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n`fastify.close()` now waits for in-flight requests on ALL dual-stack listeners (main + secondary) before resolving and running `onClose` hooks. Previously the secondary server's close callback was discarded (`close(() => {})`), so its drain was never awaited and `onClose` could release resources while a handler was still running.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n| File | Change |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `lib/server.js` | Store `{ server, closePromise }` per binding; resolve the promise in the secondary close callback |\r\n| `fastify.js` | Gate `done()` on `Promise.all` of secondary close promises; adapt `addresses()` to the new binding shape |\r\n| `test/close.test.js` | Regression test for the secondary-listener drain path |\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n- [x] `npm run unit`: full suite passes (2342 tests, 0 failures)\r\n- [x] `npm run lint`: clean\r\n- [x] `npm run coverage:ci-check-coverage`: 100% line coverage\r\n- [x] Repro: request a slow handler via the IPv4 secondary listener, call `close()` mid-request; `close()` waits (~1500ms), `onClose` fires with `inFlight = 0`\r\n\r\n## Out of scope\r\n- Single-bind (non-dual-stack) behavior is unchanged: `Promise.all([])` resolves immediately.\r\n- `forceCloseConnections` behavior is untouched.",
          "reactions": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ezefernandezyf/fastify/issues/1/reactions",
